WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.487
To understand why, the authors tracked which tokens
survived,

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:07.055
meaning they were left unchanged by the participant.

00:00:07.135 --> 00:00:10.622
Under the edit model, tokens it left un-highlighted
survived far more often,

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:14.189
about eighty-seven percent of the time,

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:17.756
while tokens it did highlight survived only about
thirty-five percent of the time.

00:00:17.836 --> 00:00:21.324
Compare that to generation-probability highlighting,

00:00:21.404 --> 00:00:24.891
where highlighted tokens still survived
seventy-four percent of the time.

00:00:24.971 --> 00:00:28.458
In other words,

00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:32.025
the edit model's highlights closely predict what
people actually change,

00:00:32.105 --> 00:00:35.593
while generation-probability highlights barely move
the needle,

00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:39.160
and all of these differences are extremely significant.
